{% extends 'help/_layout.html.twig' %}
{% block help_title %}Nutrition Goals{% endblock %}

{% block help_body %}
<figure class="figure d-block border rounded shadow-sm overflow-hidden mb-4 w-100">
    <img src="{{ asset('images/help/goals.png') }}" class="figure-img img-fluid mb-0 w-100"
         alt="The Nutrition Goals page showing a goal and its scheduled check-in">
</figure>
<p>Set a measurable nutrition goal and {{ brand.name }} checks your logged meals against it on a schedule, sending you
a progress note. It's wellness feedback, not medical advice.</p>

<h2 class="h5 fw-bold mt-4">Setting up a goal</h2>
<ol>
    <li>Go to <strong>Goals → New goal</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Chat it through</strong> — describe what you want ("eat more fiber") and the assistant turns it
        into a concrete, measurable goal — or use the structured form if you'd rather.</li>
    <li>Choose how often you want check-ins (daily or weekly), the time of day, and the format (a short
        summary, a chart, or a fuller report).</li>
    <li>Confirm, and your goal is set.</li>
</ol>

<h2 class="h5 fw-bold mt-4">Check-ins</h2>
<p>On schedule, {{ brand.name }} measures your meals against the goal and sends a progress check-in — by email and/or
text, following your <a href="{{ path('app_help_show', {topic: 'settings'}) }}">notification settings</a>. Each
goal's page keeps a history of its check-ins, status, and a trend chart.</p>
{% endblock %}

{% block help_related %}
<hr class="my-4">
<p class="small text-muted mb-1">Related:</p>
<ul class="small">
    <li><a href="{{ path('app_help_show', {topic: 'settings'}) }}">Settings &amp; Notifications</a></li>
</ul>
{% endblock %}
